    "created_at": "2017-05-04T12:51:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-04T12:51:32Z",
    "body": "> If it's at the step I'm now traversing all the documents, then couldn't one use the top level browsing context's document to achieve that kind of effect?\r\n\r\nI guess that's a good point. Only doing the traversing here for any layout-related work is clearly better than everyone doing their own traversal.\r\n\r\nIt would mean however that you get fullscreen for outer, than maybe some UI event for inner, than fullscreen for inner. Rather than all fullscreen events directly adjacent. That's probably reasonable, but if any framework is doing its own cross-document synchronizing, it's going to end up in trouble.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
