    "created_at": "2017-05-07T05:18:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-07T05:18:16Z",
    "body": "I think it makes sense to make `fullscreenchange` event for exiting fullscreen use tree order given the current spec model which has no hierarchy restriction. Using reverse tree order actually feels weird.\r\n\r\nI share the concern with @annevk that introducing this general concept might not be a good idea. Making fullscreen events not adjacent may be a problem, while I'm more worried about the order between different kinds of steps. I mean, we may want to make them dispatch in a specific order so that authors may find it easier to write handler functions modularly and performantly. For example, I have a feeling that we may actually want fullscreen events to be dispatched at a very early stage, probably even before resize, because conceptually fullscreen change can trigger some state-related DOM change, and then later handler functions can rely on that the DOM state has been changed, and just apply their size-based changes accordingly.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if this is something we should take into account, and whether authors would actually want to rely on that.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
